{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfai5q8LqvGZKhusQQ2HF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Tnf24xWiRVzDU8eEGA4AtJ","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"«WORKING_AREA»/spec.md","content":"# Spec: Dark-Mode Toggle\n\nStatus: ready-for-agent\n\n## Summary\nAdd a theme control to the Settings page that lets users choose Light, Dark, or System appearance.\n\n## Requirements\n- **Options:** `system` (default), `light`, `dark`.\n- **Default:** New and existing users start on `system`, which follows the OS `prefers-color-scheme` setting.\n- **Persistence:** Store the choice per user in their profile (e.g. `profile.theme_preference`) so it follows them across devices and sessions.\n- **Live updates:** Changing the setting applies the theme right away, with no page reload. In `system` mode, the app reacts when the OS preference changes.\n- **No flash:** Apply the resolved theme before first paint, using a cached value until the profile loads.\n\n## Implementation Notes\n- Add a nullable `theme_preference` field to the user profile, where null means `system`.\n- Expose it through the existing profile read/update API.\n- Drive styling with a `data-theme` attribute on `<html>` and CSS variables.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- The toggle shows the saved value when the Settings page loads.\n- The selection survives logout/login and works on other devices.\n- In `system` mode, the theme follows the OS setting.\n- Both themes meet WCAG AA contrast.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3675,"cache_read_input_tokens":11611,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3675},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":{"cache_miss_reason":{"type":"messages_changed","cache_missed_input_tokens":3357}},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bbbbbbbb-bbbb-4bbb-8bbb-bbbbbbbbbbbb","uuid":"54974502-74f2-4425-812e-7b4f8d8f4e79","timestamp":"2026-10-01T02:13:54.177Z","request_id":"req_011Cfai5pkmaqLcWB6T7Ui64","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01Tnf24xWiRVzDU8eEGA4AtJ":{"file_path":"«WORKING_AREA»/spec.md","content":"# Spec: Dark-Mode Toggle\n\nStatus: ready-for-agent\n\n## Summary\nAdd a theme control to the Settings page that lets users choose Light, Dark, or System appearance.\n\n## Requirements\n- **Options:** `system` (default), `light`, `dark`.\n- **Default:** New and existing users start on `system`, which follows the OS `prefers-color-scheme` setting.\n- **Persistence:** Store the choice per user in their profile (e.g. `profile.theme_preference`) so it follows them across devices and sessions.\n- **Live updates:** Changing the setting applies the theme right away, with no page reload. In `system` mode, the app reacts when the OS preference changes.\n- **No flash:** Apply the resolved theme before first paint, using a cached value until the profile loads.\n\n## Implementation Notes\n- Add a nullable `theme_preference` field to the user profile, where null means `system`.\n- Expose it through the existing profile read/update API.\n- Drive styling with a `data-theme` attribute on `<html>` and CSS variables.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- The toggle shows the saved value when the Settings page loads.\n- The selection survives logout/login and works on other devices.\n- In `system` mode, the theme follows the OS setting.\n- Both themes meet WCAG AA contrast.\n"}}}
